  "body": "Housekeeping check: the round-1 atlas review (commit `0dcd4e91`) raised 2 Major and 2 Minor findings in `atlas_reviewer/rounds.py`. A later commit, `61273b4f` (\"Let a later round approve after the prior budget fills\"), appears to address all four:\n\n- **Major** (budget overflow/superseded rounds permanently blocking approval): new tests `test_a_superseded_round_outside_the_budget_does_not_block` and `test_many_superseded_rounds_do_not_stop_a_later_approval` cover exactly this.\n- **Major** (one bad/unreadable line blocking every PR sharing the log): new `_owner()` helper attributes a bad line to its own PR, and `test_a_bad_line_blocks_only_the_pull_request_it_names` pins it.\n- **Minor** (`quote_untrusted`'s 200-char default silently truncating stored finding lines): `_q()` now passes an explicit `RECORD_CHARS` limit, with `test_a_long_finding_is_quoted_whole` covering it.\n- **Minor** (`Path.exists()` running outside the `try`, able to raise `PermissionError` and break the \"does not raise\" contract): `exists()` is now inside the `try` block in `RoundLog.read()`.\n\nI resolved those four threads on that basis. I did not resolve the two Nits (`_dropped_other` being discarded without surfacing a count, and the unused `scope=` parameter on `first_turn`) — the diff gives weaker signal on whether those were addressed, so I'm leaving them for a human or the next review round to confirm.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YR2G8DKGYvBdHioRHxxEmL\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
